*> Consumer-side contract test (T0314; specs/002-client-polish/contracts/formats-api.md "Contract tests"): the extraction
*> tool's use of the formats library, called the way the tool calls it and linked from libformats only (no extract
*> program is involved): ZIP-OPEN, ZIP-COUNT, ZIP-NAME, ZIP-FIND, ZIP-READ-RANGE and ZIP-CLOSE over a fixture
*> archive and its status words, CRC32 and its check value, SHA256-INIT/UPDATE/FINAL and the "abc" vector, FILE-WRITE,
*> FILE-READ-AT, FILE-READ-ALL and FILE-EXISTS, DIR-ENSURE, DIR-RENAME and DIR-REMOVE-TREE.
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. CONTRACT-EXTRACT-FORMATS.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 COPY FORMATS.
 01 WS-NAME                PIC X(64).
 01 WS-ROOT                PIC X(1100).
 01 WS-PATH                PIC X(1100).
 01 WS-OTHER               PIC X(1100).
 01 WS-ZIP-PATH            PIC X(1024).
 01 WS-ZIP-LENGTH          BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ZIP                 USAGE POINTER.
 01 WS-STATUS              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-COUNT               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ENTRY               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ENTRY-NAME          PIC X(256).
 01 WS-ENTRY-LENGTH        BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-BUFFER              PIC X(64).
 01 WS-CAPACITY            BINARY-LONG VALUE 64.
 01 WS-LENGTH              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-CRC                 BINARY-LONG UNSIGNED.
 01 WS-DIGEST              PIC X(32).
 01 WS-HEX                 PIC X(1024).
 01 WS-TEXT                PIC X(64).
 01 WS-OFFSET              BINARY-DOUBLE VALUE 0.
 01 WS-DATA                PIC X(12) VALUE "hello, files".
 01 WS-DATA-LENGTH         BINARY-LONG VALUE 12.
 01 WS-COMMAND             PIC X(1100).
 01 WS-SHELL               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ABC                 PIC X(3) VALUE "abc".
 01 WS-ABC-LENGTH          BINARY-LONG VALUE 3.
 01 WS-DIGITS              PIC X(9) VALUE "123456789".
 01 WS-DIGITS-LENGTH       BINARY-LONG VALUE 9.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
*>   ZIP-*: the archive the tool reads, opened, listed, searched and read by entry.
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-ZIP-PATH
     MOVE "contract/fixtures/extract/ok-small.zip" TO WS-ZIP-PATH
     MOVE FUNCTION LENGTH(FUNCTION TRIM(WS-ZIP-PATH)) TO WS-ZIP-LENGTH
     CALL "ZIP-OPEN" USING WS-ZIP-PATH WS-ZIP-LENGTH WS-ZIP WS-STATUS
     MOVE "consumer formats: ZIP-OPEN of a reject-fixture baseline gives FM-ZIP-OK" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE FM-ZIP-OK TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-STATUS TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "ZIP-COUNT" USING WS-ZIP WS-COUNT
     MOVE "consumer formats: ZIP-COUNT is 2" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 2 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-COUNT TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 2 TO WS-ENTRY
     CALL "ZIP-NAME" USING WS-ZIP WS-ENTRY WS-ENTRY-NAME WS-ENTRY-LENGTH
     MOVE "consumer formats: ZIP-NAME of entry 2" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "b.txt" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE WS-ENTRY-NAME TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "a.txt" TO WS-ENTRY-NAME
     MOVE 5 TO WS-ENTRY-LENGTH
     CALL "ZIP-FIND" USING WS-ZIP WS-ENTRY-NAME WS-ENTRY-LENGTH WS-ENTRY
     MOVE "consumer formats: ZIP-FIND of a.txt gives entry 1" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-ENTRY TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 64 TO WS-CAPACITY
     CALL "ZIP-READ-RANGE" USING WS-ZIP WS-ENTRY WS-BUFFER WS-CAPACITY WS-LENGTH WS-STATUS
     MOVE "consumer formats: ZIP-READ-RANGE inflates the deflated entry" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE FM-ZIP-OK TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-STATUS TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "consumer formats: the entry is 'hello world' (11 bytes)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "hello world" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE WS-BUFFER(1:WS-LENGTH) TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 4 TO WS-CAPACITY
     CALL "ZIP-READ-RANGE" USING WS-ZIP WS-ENTRY WS-BUFFER WS-CAPACITY WS-LENGTH WS-STATUS
     MOVE "consumer formats: a buffer too small gives FM-ZIP-CAPACITY and the size" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE FM-ZIP-CAPACITY TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-STATUS TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 11 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-LENGTH TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     MOVE "consumer formats: the size is reported (11)" TO TL-CASE
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "ZIP-CLOSE" USING WS-ZIP
     MOVE "contract/fixtures/extract/c-several-disks.zip" TO WS-ZIP-PATH
     MOVE FUNCTION LENGTH(FUNCTION TRIM(WS-ZIP-PATH)) TO WS-ZIP-LENGTH
     CALL "ZIP-OPEN" USING WS-ZIP-PATH WS-ZIP-LENGTH WS-ZIP WS-STATUS
     MOVE "consumer formats: ZIP-OPEN of several disks gives FM-ZIP-MULTI-DISK" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE FM-ZIP-MULTI-DISK TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-STATUS TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   CRC32 and SHA256-*: the check values of 22 §7.2.
     MOVE 0 TO WS-CRC
     CALL "CRC32" USING WS-DIGITS WS-DIGITS-LENGTH WS-CRC
     MOVE "consumer formats: CRC32 of 123456789 is cbf43926" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE FM-CRC-CHECK-VALUE TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-CRC TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "SHA256-INIT" USING FMSHA
     CALL "SHA256-UPDATE" USING FMSHA WS-ABC WS-ABC-LENGTH
     CALL "SHA256-FINAL" USING FMSHA WS-DIGEST
     MOVE 32 TO WS-LENGTH
     CALL "TEST-HEX-OF" USING WS-DIGEST WS-LENGTH WS-HEX
     MOVE "consumer formats: SHA-256 of abc" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "ba7816bf8f01cfea414140de5dae2223b00361a396177a9cb410ff61f20015ad" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE FUNCTION LOWER-CASE(WS-HEX(1:64)) TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   FILE-* and DIR-*: write below a made directory, read back, rename the directory, remove the tree.
     MOVE "formats-consumer" TO WS-NAME
     CALL "EXT-SCRATCH" USING WS-NAME WS-ROOT
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-COMMAND
     STRING "rm -rf " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-ROOT) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-COMMAND
     CALL "EXT-SHELL" USING WS-COMMAND WS-SHELL
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-PATH
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-ROOT) "/partial/a/b" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-PATH
     CALL "DIR-ENSURE" USING WS-PATH WS-STATUS
     MOVE "consumer formats: DIR-ENSURE makes nested directories" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE FM-OK TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-STATUS TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-PATH
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-ROOT) "/partial/a/b/file.txt" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-PATH
     CALL "FILE-WRITE" USING WS-PATH WS-DATA WS-DATA-LENGTH WS-STATUS
     MOVE "consumer formats: FILE-WRITE writes a file" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE FM-OK TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-STATUS TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 64 TO WS-LENGTH
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-TEXT
     CALL "FILE-READ-AT" USING WS-PATH WS-OFFSET WS-TEXT WS-LENGTH WS-STATUS
     MOVE "consumer formats: FILE-READ-AT reads the 12 bytes back" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 12 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-LENGTH TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-OTHER
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-ROOT) "/generated" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-OTHER
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-PATH
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-ROOT) "/partial" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-PATH
     CALL "DIR-RENAME" USING WS-PATH WS-OTHER WS-STATUS
     MOVE "consumer formats: DIR-RENAME swaps the partial directory in" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE FM-OK TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-STATUS TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "FILE-EXISTS" USING WS-PATH WS-STATUS
     MOVE "consumer formats: the partial directory is gone after the rename" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE FM-NOT-FOUND TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-STATUS TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-PATH
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-ROOT) "/generated/a/b/file.txt" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-PATH
     MOVE 64 TO WS-LENGTH
     CALL "FILE-READ-ALL" USING WS-PATH WS-ZIP-LENGTH WS-TEXT WS-CAPACITY WS-LENGTH WS-STATUS
     CALL "FILE-EXISTS" USING WS-PATH WS-STATUS
     MOVE "consumer formats: FILE-EXISTS finds the file under the new name" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE FM-OK TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-STATUS TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "DIR-REMOVE-TREE" USING WS-OTHER WS-STATUS
     MOVE "consumer formats: DIR-REMOVE-TREE removes the tree" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE FM-OK TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-STATUS TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "FILE-EXISTS" USING WS-OTHER WS-STATUS
     MOVE "consumer formats: nothing is left" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE FM-NOT-FOUND TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-STATUS TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     STOP RUN.
 END PROGRAM CONTRACT-EXTRACT-FORMATS.

 COPY EXTEST.

*> TEST-HEX-OF: lower-case hex of up to 512 bytes (the helper of formats/tests/FMTEST.cpy, kept here so the test links
*> against the libraries only).
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-HEX-OF.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 01 WS-I                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 B-AREA                 PIC X(512) BASED.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 01 L-AREA                 PIC X.
 01 L-COUNT                BINARY-LONG.
 01 L-HEX                  PIC X(1024).
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING L-AREA L-COUNT L-HEX.
     SET ADDRESS OF B-AREA TO ADDRESS OF L-AREA
     MOVE SPACES TO L-HEX
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > L-COUNT
         MOVE FUNCTION LOWER-CASE(FUNCTION HEX-OF(B-AREA(WS-I:1))) TO L-HEX(WS-I * 2 - 1:2)
     END-PERFORM
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM TEST-HEX-OF.
